  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 7508.05 Warning Notice",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-03-24",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 7508.05 Warning Notice.\n\n(a) The department shall, absent any computer failure, mail warning letters through first class United States mail to individuals as they accumulate point system convictions.\n\n(b) Notwithstanding (a) above, failure of a person to receive such a letter shall not prohibit further action against the person's license.\n\nSource. #6337, eff 9-25-96 (from Saf-C 211.05); ss by #8174, INTERIM, eff 9-25-04, EXPIRES: 3-24-05; ss by #8230-B, eff 12-17-04; ss by #10395-B, eff 8-15-13; ss by #13938, eff 4-24-24 (formerly Saf-C 212.05) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 7500)",
